<p><strong>Processing numbers with multiple digits</strong><br>
Another complexity in this expression is that some numbers have multiple di=
gits. We=E2=80=99ll need a way to build numbers digit by digit until we rea=
ch the end of the number. We can build a number using the variable <code>cu=
rr_num</code>, which is initially set to 0. Every time we encounter a new d=
igit, we multiply <code>curr_num</code> by 10 and add the new digit to it, =
effectively shifting all digits to the left and appending the new digit.</p=
